course: dictionary
lesson: 3209
title: Describing fun: enjoyable
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Enjoyable means giving you pleasure: something fun or nice to do, see or have. Read it in the sentence: «We had an enjoyable day at the seaside.» The day was fun, so enjoyable means fun.
explain: Look at its parts. Enjoy is a whole word, and -able usually follows a whole word, so enjoy + able makes enjoyable. The idea is "able to be enjoyed", which is why it means fun.
explain: Use it for things you like: «an enjoyable trip», «make it more enjoyable», «thoroughly enjoyable». Thoroughly means completely, so thoroughly enjoyable means very, very fun.
fact: Enjoyable means giving pleasure; fun or nice to do, see or have.
fact: «An enjoyable day» means a day full of fun.
fact: Enjoy is a whole word, so -able follows it: enjoy + able = enjoyable.
fact: Like other adjectives, it can change: more enjoyable, most enjoyable.
fact: «Thoroughly enjoyable» means completely fun, because thoroughly means completely.
exercise: «We had an enjoyable day at the zoo.» What does enjoyable mean here? | *Full of fun and pleasure | Very tiring and long | Cold and wet | Quiet and empty
exercise: Which word is made from the whole word enjoy with -able added? | enjoyful | enjoyness | *enjoyable | enjoyible
exercise: «The film was thoroughly enjoyable, and we laughed all the way through.» Which word has a meaning closest to enjoyable? | Boring | *Pleasant | Frightening | Expensive
test: Maya says, «Let's make the trip more enjoyable.» What does more enjoyable mean? | Most boring | Smaller | Less fun | *Giving more pleasure
test: Which idea would make a long car journey more enjoyable? | Turn off every light | Stop talking to everyone | *Play a game together | Skip every stop
exam: The picnic was so ___ that nobody wanted to go home. | Muddy | Empty | Tiring | *Enjoyable
